  "rationale": "The batch repeatedly predicts a determiner instead of a proper noun after introductory “with”, and gives very low probability to proper nouns after introductory clauses ending in a comma. The revealed stories support a reusable continuation pattern: a person name can follow terminal “with” or a terminal comma. Add equal contextual evidence to the available name tokens rather than encoding one observed name as the expected continuation. Names remain uncertain among the alternatives. This may overpredict names after commas or “with” in other contexts; the replay gate must assess that risk, and this patch has not been validated.",
